# tools/enhancements-test.js opens with Chinese-heavy comment blocks: the first
# 8 KB cross git's binary-sniffing threshold in the C locale (ls-files --eol
# reported "-text"), which disabled CRLF normalization for that one file — every
# edit then showed up in `git diff --check` as trailing whitespace (the CR of
# each added CRLF line). Declaring it text restores the same treatment every
# other file gets: LF in the index, CRLF in the worktree.
tools/enhancements-test.js text
